{
  "kind": "cast8",
  "comment": "Pose guides for the 8-direction, 6-frame cast sheet; conventions as walk8.json. Six frames of gather, raise, overhead build, peak, release and settle. The build is vertical rather than forward on purpose: height reads in every one of the eight rows, where a forward reach reads in none of the ones facing the camera. At the peak the hands are above the head circle and the spine is arched slightly back; the release pitches the torso forward over a bent front knee and throws both hands out at chest height, which is the single frame that changes silhouette enough to read as the spell leaving.",
